Solar AI Ops — Development Roadmap

Solar AI Ops is an early-stage open-source initiative focused on applying artificial intelligence to photovoltaic system monitoring, diagnostics and solar operations.

This roadmap describes the initial direction of the project. Priorities may evolve as the architecture is developed and the community provides feedback.

Phase 1 — Foundation

Goal: Establish the technical foundation and define the first open data structures.

* Define the initial software architecture
* Define standardized photovoltaic system data models
* Create anonymized or synthetic sample datasets
* Document common solar monitoring scenarios
* Define expected-generation and actual-generation structures
* Establish repository standards
* Add contribution guidelines
* Define the first API specifications

Phase 2 — Monitoring Intelligence

Goal: Develop the first operational monitoring components.

Planned capabilities:

* Detect offline photovoltaic systems
* Identify communication failures
* Detect abnormal generation patterns
* Compare actual generation against expected generation
* Identify systems with potential underperformance
* Classify operational alerts
* Prioritize systems requiring technical attention

The initial implementation should remain platform-independent whenever possible.

Phase 3 — Energy Data Analysis

Goal: Combine photovoltaic production information with energy-consumption and utility data.

Planned capabilities:

* Import generation history
* Process energy-bill data
* Compare generated, injected and compensated energy
* Analyze consumption patterns
* Detect inconsistencies between monitoring and utility information
* Generate standardized performance indicators

Phase 4 — AI-Assisted Diagnostics

Goal: Use AI to help transform operational data into understandable technical information.

Planned capabilities:

* AI-assisted technical diagnostics
* Explain detected anomalies
* Suggest investigation priorities
* Generate technical performance summaries
* Assist technical-support workflows
* Natural-language queries over operational data

AI recommendations should assist rather than replace technical validation.

Phase 5 — Connectors and Integrations

Goal: Allow the community to connect different platforms and business systems.

Planned components:

* Monitoring-platform connector interface
* REST API
* Webhook support
* CRM integrations
* Service-management integrations
* Community-developed connectors

Vendor-specific connectors should remain modular so that the core project does not depend on a single manufacturer or monitoring platform.

Phase 6 — Community and Ecosystem

Goal: Make Solar AI Ops easier to adopt and extend.

* Developer documentation
* Installation guides
* Example implementations
* Contribution templates
* Automated testing
* Containerized deployment
* Community connector directory
* Versioned releases

Current Priority

The current priority is Phase 1.

The immediate objective is to establish a clean technical foundation before implementing production integrations.

Contributions, technical discussions and architecture suggestions are welcome.
